{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>מתהלך</b> — defective [in its root], or it serves like the kaf of איש משרת, in place of the kaf corresponding to the warned son. I shall explain the third part — this part — it is possible that it is a separate book in its own right among the books of Solomon, and the wise men of Hezekiah transcribed his pleasant proverbs and joined them with these."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The text of the first sentence is opaque; 'חסר או משרת' is rendered hyper-literally. The referent of 'כאיש משרת' is uncertain and the syntax of the second clause is difficult."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:34.794097184Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}